Description: Provides programmatic access, local caching, spatial subsetting,
    temporal aggregation, anomaly computation, and validation metrics for the
    Peruvian Interpolated data of SENAMHI's Climatological and hydrological
    Observations (PISCO). Specifically supports PISCOp v3.0 (1981-2025)
    gridded daily ('PISCOp_d.nc'), monthly ('PISCOp_m.nc'), and climatological
    normal ('PISCOp_clim2.nc') rainfall datasets developed by SENAMHI and
    hosted on Figshare <doi:10.6084/m9.figshare.32411886>. Includes optimized
    workflows for basin-scale extraction, seasonal aggregations (SENAMHI wet
    and dry seasons), and spatial raster processing based on 'terra' and 'sf'.
